the investigation into the deadly mass  shooting at one of the nation's largest  breweries is now focused on a home on  Milwaukee's North Side a heavy police  presence was reported there overnight  police say a 51 year old employee killed  five co workers before taking his own  life  SWAT teams quickly responded to the  sprawling Molson Coors complex yesterday  after receiving emergency calls Dean  Reynolds has more from Milwaukee at 2:08  p.m. yesterday police and fire rescue  from Milwaukee and surrounding areas  rushed to the Molson Coors plant  following reports of an active shooter  wearing bulletproof vests and heavily  armed they FBI and ATF agents stormed  the campus searching for the gunman  nearby schools and businesses were  placed on lockdown as dozens of officers  cleared each building on a campus where  around a thousand people work we're all  pretty scared I mean we were watching  the live streams on TV try and see what  was going on outside because we can see  anything about five hours after the  shooting began investigators confirmed  the gunmen killed five people before  turning the gun on himself this is an  unspeakable tragedy for our city this is  a community tragedy and as we grieve for  these families we must remember the  sacrifices that they made as police  cleared the scene employees on the  campus were allowed to leave one by one  to reunite with their families I  wouldn't go on to talk to this guy there  it was relieving me I'd be one of them  guys yeah I know that for a fact because  I would have walked right into what was  going on Randy Chenoweth has worked as a  utilities operator at the plant for 42  years he says he was in an office just  15 to 20 feet away from the gunshots  during his shift change I know some of  the victims and I really feel for the  families pray for you it's all I can  really do Dean Reynolds reporting from  Milwaukee Forrest Dean thank you very  much
 

